updated=updated.replace("games 14–15 lost, and game 16 drew. The 20k record is three wins, eight losses and one draw.","games 14–15 lost, game 16 drew, and game 17 won. The 20k record is four wins, eight losses and one draw.");
const r16link="- Read game-016.md for the latest review; game-016.sgf and game-016-log.json contain all 51 moves (48 stone moves, three passes), all 26 returned positions with inventories, early counts, the corrected F1/G1 connection mistake, explicit C1/D2 life proof and independent 44–37 area count after marking the five dead right stones.";
updated=updated.replace(r16link,r16link.replace("the latest review","its review")+"\n- Read game-017.md for the latest review; game-017.sgf and game-017-log.json contain all 87 moves (85 stone moves, two passes), all 44 returned play positions with group/liberty inventories, early/late counts, the two-stone versus one-stone J1 recapture distinction, explicit life proofs and verified 48–33 area.");
const newLessons=`63. Game 17 developed C3/G7/G3 footholds, then F2/G2/E2/D3 actually connected the lower stones. Its move-14 unsecured lower 25 plus upper-right 16 target was only 41. G5/H5/J5 expanded the upper boundary; no opening move is established as best. An early second foothold supplied a viable base instead of a late unsupported invasion.
64. Game 17's upper life required H8/H9 to prevent G9 and J8 from joining, J7 to atari J8, and H7 to connect isolated J7 (which had only H7/J6). J9 captured J8; H6 captured invading J6. Final true J6 (H6/J5/J7) and J8 (H8/J7/J9) had one connected Black boundary group. Later F5/E6/F6 expanded this living upper region from fifteen to eighteen.
65. Game 17's B5 left White A3/A4/A5 only A6; W B6 ignored the atari. B A6 captured three, but W A7 left isolated A6 only A5, so A5 immediately connected it through B5. F5 left W F6 only E6; W H1 ignored it. E6 captured F6, but W D6 left E6 only F6, so F6 immediately connected through F5/F7/G6. Capturing and then connecting were separate required steps. These gains depended on actual ignored ataris.
66. Game 17's first two B J1 captures removed W G1/H1 and left J1 only H1; W H1 legally captured J1 and had G1/J1. This was not ko, because two captured White stones were not restored. After B G1 connected through F1/G2, W H1 had only J1. B J1 then captured ONE stone; immediate W H1 would restore the board and was forbidden by simple ko. W C9 played elsewhere; B H1 connected J1. This transient ko is manually inferred, not a returned ko marker. No immediate recapture was attempted.
67. Game 17 counted contested D4/G1 separately: lower 28 plus upper 18 target =46; losing both would draw at44. D4/G1 were secured, then H1/J1 added two for48. Final lower 25 stones plus five territory =30, upper16 plus J6/J8 =18. Lower true C2 (B2/C1/C3/D2) and E1 (D1/E2/F1) were connected before final A1 cleanup. The verified B+8 does not validate the ignored-atari gains as forced.

`;
updated=updated.replace("## Next-game focus",newLessons+"## Next-game focus");
updated=updated.replace("- Choose a rank deliberately. Retain 20k until living groups and scored wins are repeatable. Game 16 drew with 37 living left area and a failed right invasion; the 20k record is three wins, eight losses and one draw. 9d remains the target.","- Choose a rank deliberately. Retain 20k until living groups and scored wins are repeatable. Game 17 won B+8 with 30 lower plus 18 upper area, following game 16's draw. The 20k record is four wins, eight losses and one draw. Important gains still relied on ignored ataris; 9d remains the target.\n- Keep game 17's two early footholds and explicit life proofs: lower C2/E1, upper J6/J8. H7 joined short-liberty J7 before the upper capture; A5 joined A6 and F6 joined E6 immediately after opponent ataris. A capture is not finished until the new stones are safe.\n- Count contested boundary points separately, as with game 17's D4/G1. The 46-point target would draw if both were lost; securing them and H1/J1 produced48. Continue counting around moves10–16, and seek a margin beyond45 as Black.\n- Re-read game 17's right corner before using any recapture idea: two-stone J1 captures permitted W H1 recapture with two liberties; the later one-stone capture became ko only after G1 was Black. Rebuild the board and compare the actual recapture, rather than labeling every one-liberty capturer a ko.");
updated=updated.replace("- Continue at 20k. Games 10–11 and 13 won, but important captures relied on opponent errors;","- Continue at 20k. Games 10–11, 13 and 17 won, but important captures relied on opponent errors;");
if(updated===old)throw Error("No updates");
text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: AGENTS.md\n@@\n"+old.trimEnd().split("\n").map(l=>"-"+l).join("\n")+"\n"+updated.trimEnd().split("\n").map(l=>"+"+l).join("\n")+"\n*** End Patch"));
store("agents17new",updated);
text(await tools.mcp__desk__list_files({}));

